    year = {2022},
    doi = {10.4324/9781003090946},
    note = {SUMMARY: Edited volume (CrossRef lists the two editors as authors) offering new perspectives on the theoretical elements of the Opus postumum, which it reads as central to the relation between Kant's transcendental philosophy and his natural philosophy, practical philosophy, philosophy of religion and metaphysics, and as showing Kant correcting and developing the critical philosophy. Chapters address the transition from the Metaphysical Foundations of Natural Science to physics as an answer to a deficiency in critical thought, the ether and its transcendental deduction, self-affection and the self-positing of the subject, and the idea of God in the highest standpoint of transcendental philosophy (publisher abstract). SUBFIELD AND DEBATE: Opus postumum: the transition project, the ether proofs and the Selbstsetzungslehre, and the unity of the critical system. SIGNIFICANCE INDICATORS: CrossRef is-referenced-by-count 0 and S2 citations 0 (retrieved 2026-10-01). Publisher: Routledge. SEP: cited in the kant-science entry bibliography (dated 2023). No review found by CrossRef search. YEAR NOTE: CrossRef gives online publication 2022-09-28 and no print date, and S2 gives 2022, while the SEP bibliography dates the volume 2023; dated 2022 here, so check against a 2023 duplicate.},
    keywords = {kant, opus-postumum, tp-science-math, debate-other-transition, type-edited-volume, Medium, summary-source-abstract}
}

